      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Carmen cuts a piece of drill fabric with a length of $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}$ to make a tablecloth. If the fabric has a width of $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m},$ what will be the area of the tablecloth? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe tablecloth will have an area of\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The tablecloth will have an area of $(2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\times 1\\,\\frac{1}{2}){\\text{m}}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we write $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(1\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{9\\times 3}{4\\times 2}=\\frac{27}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{8}=3\\,\\text{R}3=3\\,\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$",
